<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bevagna</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mevania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bevagna, the ancient Mevania, is a small town in the Umbrian plain of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the route of the Roman Via Flaminia. An Umbrian community and then a Roman municipium, it preserves a Roman mosaic of sea creatures and the remains of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>. It later came under papal rule and keeps much of its medieval centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bevagna.jpg" alt="Bevagna" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagai Agmon-Snir حچاي اچمون-سنير חגי אגמון-שניר · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BevagnaDec122023_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
